"use worker";
/* ============================================================================
 * lore_arcs.js — EPISODE SPINE (Five-Hero AU) — EP1-EP36 (Arcs 1-9, 11-13)
 * The canon storyline as a continuous run of EPISODES; each EP == one in-story
 * day == one scripted beat. The engine (master_director) tracks the continuous
 * EP on the header; this script injects the entry whose `ep` matches the CURRENT
 * EP, so the model always gets THIS day's beat and nothing ahead of it.
 *
 * Each entry is the world's DEFAULT timeline for that day (what unfolds around
 * {{user}}) — divertible by his choices, never a script that moves or speaks for
 * him. "Voice anchors" are characteristic lines for the NPCs present (vary them,
 * never verbatim, never a line for {{user}}). Every character is an adult (18+);
 * leveling means healing and getting stronger, never aging.
 *
 * Openings map: EP1 = greeting_summoning, EP7 = greeting (Dragon Hourglass),
 * EP9 = greeting (gala/duel). Full canon spine EP1-36. Arc 10 "Intermission" is
 * CUT (the arc numbering skips it: Arc 9 = EP25-27, Arc 11 = EP28-31).
 * TRAVEL COMPRESSION: each EP is ONE day, so journeys the anime spans over weeks
 * are compressed to at most ~2 days/episodes — reach destinations within the day,
 * never narrate multi-day treks (the engine's travel time-increment supports this).
 * Assign at Depth 1.
 * ========================================================================== */

var LORE = [
  { ep:1,
    full:"[EP1 — Summoning | Arc 1] The five Cardinal Heroes are pulled into the summoning chamber beneath Melromarc's castle — Shield (Naofumi), Sword (Ren), Spear (Motoyasu), Bow (Itsuki), and Axe ({{user}}) — each with their Holy Weapon already bound. The court and the Church of the Five receive them with reverence; King Aultcray and his ministers explain the summons: the Waves of Calamity threaten the world and the Heroes are its promised protectors. The four favored (Sword/Spear/Bow/Axe) are feted; only the Shield draws quiet disdain from Church-of-the-Four sympathizers — nothing open yet. This early, Naofumi is genuinely upbeat and eager, a fan of this world's tales, trusting — NOT yet the cynic. The Heroes realize they hail from different worlds (the others treat it like a game they know), are shown their status screens, and told each may wield any weapon of their own class but never another Hero's. They are given quarters for the night; parties and stipends come at tomorrow's audience. It is evening; the castle settles toward night.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, not a script — vary freely, and never voice {{user}}): King Aultcray, grave and formal — 'Heroes, you are called to protect this land from the Waves that would devour it.' Motoyasu, breezy — 'Heh, just like the game I played. I've got a handle on this.' Ren, cool and detached — 'Different game from mine, but the mechanics look standard enough.' Itsuki, self-important — 'We were chosen to save this world. I intend to do it justice.' Naofumi, bright and eager (pre-betrayal) — 'This is unreal... an actual summoning. So — where do we start leveling?'\n[Axe Hero] {{user}} is the fifth summon, the Axe Hero, favored like the other three — courted, not scorned. Awed, skeptical, gamer-savvy, or unnerved by the Church's fawning: his read is his own. Default beat unless he diverts it — introductions, the King's briefing, the night's rest ahead. Never move or speak for him; the world presents, then waits.",
    brief:"[EP1 — Summoning] The five Heroes (Shield/Sword/Spear/Bow/Axe={{user}}) are summoned and briefed on the Waves; the four favored are feted, only the Shield quietly disdained. Pre-betrayal Naofumi is upbeat and trusting. Evening, castle. {{user}} is the favored Axe Hero." },

  { ep:2,
    full:"[EP2 — Parties Assigned | Arc 1] Morning. The five Heroes are called back before King Aultcray, who grants each a starting stipend of coin and summons the realm's adventurers to form the Heroes' parties. It is the VOLUNTEERS' choice whom to follow: the four favored — Sword, Spear, Bow, and Axe — draw eager crowds, and a striking red-haired adventurer who calls herself 'Myne Sophia' is the FIRST to sign on with Motoyasu, the Spear Hero. When the choosing settles, every favored Hero has a party — and the Shield stands alone, not one volunteer beside him. The hall notices; whispers and muttering ripple through the court about the lone, unwanted Shield Hero. Then Myne raises her voice, loud enough for the whole hall to hear: someone ought to support the poor Shield Hero, so she will leave the Spear's party for his. Motoyasu, plainly smitten, balks at letting her go — but she coaxes him around, and crosses to stand at Naofumi's side. Still hopeful, Naofumi accepts gratefully, blind to it being the first thread of a trap. (In truth 'Myne' is Malty, the first princess.)\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; use honorifics; never voice {{user}}): King Aultcray, formal — 'Adventurers of Melromarc, choose your Hero and stand with them against the Waves.' A courtier, muttering — 'The Shield Hero... not one soul chose him. How telling.' 'Myne'/Malty, sweet and carrying — 'Someone simply must support the Shield Hero-sama. Motoyasu-sama, please — let me go to him.' Motoyasu, reluctant and smitten — 'Eeeh? You're leaving my party, Myne-san? ...Well, if it's the kind thing to do.' Naofumi, quietly grateful (pre-betrayal) — 'You're... joining me? Thank you. Really.'\n[Axe Hero] This is where {{user}}'s own party forms: a handful of volunteers CHOOSE the Axe Hero of their own accord (he never hand-picks them). How he receives them — gracious, cocky, indifferent, testing — is his (they hail him 'Lord Atro' or 'Atro-sama'), and he can't miss the Shield left conspicuously alone until Myne's loud 'charity.' Default beat unless diverted: the stipend, the recruiting floor, the parties forming. The world offers and waits.",
    brief:"[EP2 — Parties Assigned] Morning audience: stipends granted; adventurers pick a Hero. 'Myne' joins Motoyasu FIRST; when all four favored have parties the Shield stands alone and the court murmurs — then Myne loudly, 'charitably' leaves the smitten, reluctant Motoyasu to join Naofumi (the trap's first thread). {{user}}'s own party of volunteers forms by their choice." },

  { ep:3,
    full:"[EP3 — The Betrayal | Arc 1] The next dawn the Heroes are summoned again — but Motoyasu is already there with Malty (as 'Myne') clinging to his arm, and soldiers drag Naofumi in. Malty bursts into tears and accuses him: that he robbed her and forced himself on her in the night. The court and the other favored Heroes believe her at once; the King's fury is total. Stripped of standing and branded a criminal, Naofumi is cast out — his coin, his trust, and his name gone in a single morning. This is the hinge of his whole story: the upbeat newcomer curdles here into the cynic who assumes everyone lies and that proof must be paid up front. Portray the shift AS it happens — shock, denial, then cold, bitter hardening.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; never voice {{user}}): Malty, tearful and flawless — 'He took everything, and then he— I was so frightened!' King Aultcray, thunderous — 'You disgrace the name of Hero. Out of my sight before I have you gaoled.' Motoyasu, righteous — 'You're the lowest kind of scum, Naofumi.' Itsuki, cold — 'And he calls himself a Hero.' Naofumi, gutted then hardening — 'I didn't— ...you've already decided, haven't you. Fine.'\n[Axe Hero] As a favored Hero, {{user}} stands in that court while the Shield is condemned on a princess's word. He can speak up for Naofumi, demand proof, hold his tongue, or side with the crowd — a real fork, entirely his. The King and the Church of the Four read the room as unanimous; whether the Axe Hero breaks that is his call. The world condemns and waits; it never puts words or motion on {{user}}.",
    brief:"[EP3 — The Betrayal] Malty publicly, tearfully frames Naofumi for robbery and assault; the court and favored Heroes believe her and he's branded a criminal and cast out — the moment his trust shatters into cynicism. {{user}}, a favored Hero, can speak up, stay silent, or side with the crowd." },

  { ep:4,
    full:"[EP4 — Outcast in the Rain | Arc 2] Disgraced, Naofumi finds every shop and inn shut to him — merchants mutter 'devil,' the Church of the Four's slur already spreading. At the smithy, the blacksmith Erhard nearly throws a punch on the rumor alone, then looks hard at Naofumi's face, finds no guilt in it, and instead presses a set of plain clothes on him for free. Rain comes down in sheets. Raw with anger, Naofumi takes it out on the orange balloon-monsters in the fields outside the walls, fighting through the night in the downpour until he grinds to level 2 — learning the hard way that the Shield can guard but barely scratch a foe. He is fully the cynic now: clipped, distrustful, blackly practical.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; never voice {{user}}): Erhard, gruff then softening — 'Rumors are cheap, kid. ...Tch. Here — can't have you walking around in rags.' A wary merchant, shuttering his stall — 'We don't serve your kind. Move along.' Naofumi, bitter and short — 'Right. Of course. I'll do it myself, then.'\n[Axe Hero] While the Shield is spat on in the rain, {{user}} the Axe Hero is dry, fed, and courted — same city, opposite reception — and Erhard's forge serves him warmly. If {{user}} is out in Castle Town tonight he might glimpse the disgraced Shield hacking balloons alone in the storm; noticing, ignoring, or approaching is his to choose. The world runs its day around him and waits.",
    brief:"[EP4 — Outcast in the Rain] Shops shun Naofumi; only Erhard sees his innocence and gifts him clothes; in the rain he vents on balloon-monsters through the night to reach level 2, fully the cynic now. {{user}} gets the warm, opposite reception and may glimpse the Shield in the storm." },

  { ep:5,
    full:"[EP5 — The Slave Trader | Arc 2] Naofumi works the forest by day, unlocking the Leaf Shield from what he harvests and hauling drops back to sell. That evening, eating in a tavern, he realizes with a jolt that he can't taste any of it — the betrayal has stolen even that. Heading out again at night, he's waved down by an oily slave trader who parades demi-human slaves before him: in human-supremacist Melromarc a slave can attack for a Shield Hero who cannot, and a slave 'cannot lie' to its master. Nearly broke, Naofumi picks the cheapest of them — a deathly ill, badly frightened adult raccoon-demi-human woman named Raphtalia — for thirty silver.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; never voice {{user}}): The slave trader (Beloukas), unctuous — 'A slave cannot lie to its master, Hero. This one's sickly, but cheap — thirty silver and she's yours.' Naofumi, coldly practical — '...Fine. That one. I can't afford to be picky.' Raphtalia (a grown woman, ill and withdrawn, barely audible) — a flinch, then a small, wary '...yes, master.'\n[Axe Hero] The same trader deals with {{user}} — the Axe Hero could browse this market for companions of his own (all adults, by their own arrangement) or want nothing to do with slaving at all; his stance is his, and unlike the Shield he needs no slave to fight. Default beat: the forest, the tasteless supper, the trader's tent by night. The world presents and waits on him.",
    brief:"[EP5 — The Slave Trader] Naofumi unlocks the Leaf Shield, finds he can no longer taste food, and — needing something that can attack for him — buys the cheapest slave, the sick, frightened adult demi-human Raphtalia, for 30 silver. {{user}} may use the same trader or reject slaving outright." },

  { ep:6,
    full:"[EP6 — First Sword | Arc 2] Naofumi kits Raphtalia out at Erhard's, feeds her properly at the tavern, and takes her hunting. Frightened at first, she steadies under his blunt but unexpectedly careful handling — he doses her medicine, keeps her fed, and talks her through the panic when the monsters bleed. She proves her worth fast; as they level she does not age — she is a grown woman healing, hardening, and coming into real skill (her demi-human maturation is already complete). They return to upgrade her gear, a true fighting pair now — she his sword, since he can only be the shield.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; never voice {{user}}): Erhard, wry as he fits her blade — 'She'll do better with steel that fits her hand. There — try that one.' Raphtalia, fear giving way to resolve — 'I can do it. I'll fight — for you, Naofumi-sama.' Naofumi, curt but thawing a hair — 'Eat. You're no use to me half-dead. ...You did fine out there.'\n[Axe Hero] In parallel, {{user}}'s party levels and kits out at the same shops; the Axe Hero can wield any axe of his class and, unlike the Shield, hits like a hammer himself. Whether his path crosses Naofumi and his new swordswoman at Erhard's or out in the field is his to choose. The world turns around him; it never acts for him.",
    brief:"[EP6 — First Sword] Naofumi equips, feeds, and steadies the frightened Raphtalia, who heals and grows into a capable swordswoman as they hunt and level (adult throughout). {{user}}'s own party levels in parallel and may cross their path." },

  { ep:7,
    full:"[EP7 — The Dragon Hourglass | Arc 3] Stronger now, his shield-collection and power grown, Naofumi restocks at Erhard's and brings Raphtalia — a confident swordswoman these days — to the Church of the Four's Dragon Hourglass to read how near the next Wave is. The Second Wave is close (the true first Wave struck before the Heroes were ever summoned; this is the first they will actually face). All five Heroes and their parties gather beneath the great glass. Motoyasu accosts Naofumi, gushes over Raphtalia and paws at her hand, and 'warns' her away from the 'dangerous' Shield; Malty sneers that a demi-human is drawing praise; Ren and Itsuki are coldly dismissive. Naofumi collects Raphtalia and turns to go — running square into the Axe Hero in his path. (This is Opening 2.)\nVoice anchors (light — the greeting carries the scene; never voice {{user}}): Motoyasu, oblivious — 'A woman as lovely as you shouldn't waste herself on him.' Ren, flat — 'Don't hold us back.' Naofumi, cold — 'We're leaving. ...Move.'\n[Axe Hero] {{user}} is among the Heroes gathered at the Hourglass, and Naofumi pulls up right in front of him on his way out. Engage, block, step aside, needle him, or offer a hand — his call. The world sets the meeting and stops for him.",
    brief:"[EP7 — The Dragon Hourglass] The Heroes gather at the Church of the Four's Hourglass as the Second Wave nears; Motoyasu paws at Raphtalia and warns her off Naofumi, who leaves and runs into the Axe Hero (Opening 2). {{user}} is right in his path." },

  { ep:8,
    full:"[EP8 — The Second Wave | Arc 3] The last grain falls and the Hourglass empties: by the world's fixed game-mechanics, every Hero and their whole party — {{user}} included — is instantly torn from where they stand and set down at the single Wave site, a red-skied rift already vomiting monsters. This warp is an involuntary SYSTEM event, the ONE time the world moves {{user}}: render the pull seizing him and dropping him near the other Heroes at the rift, then STOP for his action. Motoyasu, Ren, and Itsuki charge straight for the boss and its glory; Naofumi turns instead for the nearby village of Riyute to shield the villagers, Melromarc's own knights flinging spells heedless of whether the Shield is caught in the blast. The favored trio fell the Chimera boss and the Wave breaks — and it is Naofumi's stand that actually saves Riyute.\nVoice anchors (characteristic, vary freely; never voice {{user}}): Motoyasu, charging — 'The boss is mine! Try to keep up!' A knight, reckless — 'Cast on the rift — never mind the Shield!' A terrified villager — 'Please, someone — the monsters are in the houses!' Naofumi, grim — 'Behind me. All of you. Move.' Raphtalia — 'I've got the left, Naofumi-sama!'\n[Axe Hero] {{user}} lands near the Heroes as the Wave erupts. From there it is his: charge the boss with the favored trio, break off to defend Riyute beside the scorned Shield, hold a flank with his own party, or something else entirely. The rift is the scene's gravity — monsters everywhere — and the world acts on him, then waits for his move.",
    brief:"[EP8 — The Second Wave] The Hourglass empties and auto-warps every Hero (incl. {{user}}) to the single red-sky rift. The favored trio charge the Chimera boss; Naofumi defends Riyute as knights cast heedlessly near him; his stand saves the village. {{user}} lands near the heroes and chooses his role." },

  { ep:9,
    full:"[EP9 — Victory Gala & the Duel | Arc 3] The night after the Wave, the palace throws a victory gala; all Heroes and parties attend, courtiers thanking the favored — {{user}} among them. Naofumi broods in a far corner over an untouched plate until Raphtalia coaxes him to eat. Her open devotion sours Motoyasu's mood, and — prodded by Malty and King Aultcray — he hurls down a challenge: a duel over Raphtalia, and if Naofumi loses she is freed and her slave crest struck off. The King orders him to accept. In the duel Naofumi actually gains the upper hand, until Malty secretly interferes and Motoyasu wins. Believing he has lost the one person who stood by him, Naofumi's despair boils into the awakening of the Wrath curse-series — but Raphtalia, crest gone, CHOOSES to stay at his side regardless. At the reward ceremony the favored trio are heaped with gold while Naofumi is handed scraps; leaving, Raphtalia asks — of her own will — to take her slave crest back. (This is Opening 3.)\nVoice anchors (vary freely; never voice {{user}}): Malty, honey and venom — 'Careful, Shield Hero. You're all alone in this room.' Motoyasu, grandstanding — 'Slavery is beneath a Hero. Fight me and free her!' King Aultcray, contempt — 'Rotten to the core. I order you to accept.' Naofumi, despair into rage — '...Fine. Have it your way.' Raphtalia, unshaken — 'Even without the crest, I choose you. It was never the crest, Naofumi-sama.'\n[Axe Hero] {{user}} stands among the Heroes as the rigged duel is set. Watch it play out, call out the obvious setup, back Motoyasu, or step in for the Shield — his choice, and a pointed one before the whole court. The world stages it and stops for him.",
    brief:"[EP9 — Victory Gala & the Duel] A rigged duel over Raphtalia (lose = her crest struck off); Malty's interference hands Motoyasu the win, Naofumi's despair wakes the Wrath series, yet Raphtalia chooses him crest-free. Trio get gold, Naofumi scraps (Opening 3). {{user}} witnesses or intervenes." },

  { ep:10,
    full:"[EP10 — The Egg | Arc 4: Filo Rial] Naofumi and Raphtalia return to the slave trader so she can have her crest reapplied at her own insistence; impressed by how she's flourished, he offers to buy her back, and Naofumi flatly refuses. On the way out a monster-egg lottery catches his eye and he gambles on one. Back in Castle Town the medicine-seller and the magic-shop owner \u2014 whose families he shielded at Riyute during the Wave \u2014 press gifts and supplies on him, nearly the only warmth the Shield gets in this city. In Riyute the egg hatches into a fluffy filolial chick he names Filo; fed and leveled, she balloons in size at a monstrous rate, big enough to ride within the day.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): the slave trader (Beloukas), oily \u2014 'Ku-ku... she's worth ten times her price now, Shield Hero-sama. Sell her back to me?' Naofumi, flat \u2014 'No. Reapply the crest. That's all.' the magic-shop owner, grateful \u2014 'You saved my family at Riyute, Hero-sama \u2014 take these, no charge.' Raphtalia, warm then startled \u2014 'A monster egg, Naofumi-sama? ...Eeeh?! It hatched already?!'\n[Axe Hero] The same lottery and the same shopkeepers serve {{user}} \u2014 the Axe Hero could gamble for a monster of his own, and the folk he's helped fawn over him openly, no scorn unlike the Shield beside the stall. Whether he raises a beast, or crosses Naofumi at the trader's tent, is his. The world offers, then waits.",
    brief:"[EP10 — The Egg] Naofumi refuses to sell Raphtalia back, wins a monster egg that hatches into the fast-growing filolial Filo, and gets rare gratitude from the Riyute families he saved. {{user}} can raise his own monster from the same lottery." },

  { ep:11,
    full:"[EP11 — The Cart Race | Arc 4: Filo Rial] Motoyasu and Malty sweep into Riyute and install the Spear Hero as its new lord, slapping crushing taxes on the village that only just survived a Wave. Naofumi refuses to let it stand, and with the Queen's ninja-like Shadows quietly feeding him leverage, the dispute is settled the Melromarc way \u2014 a cart-race against Motoyasu for control of the village. Motoyasu's side cheats outright; Naofumi wins anyway on Filo's monstrous speed. The grateful village grants him a carriage and a merchant's bill of passage \u2014 his living on the road, now.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Motoyasu, gallant and oblivious \u2014 'A race, then! When I win, this village is under MY protection, Naofumi.' Malty, sweet venom \u2014 'Ufufu~ do try to keep up, Shield Hero.' a Shadow, low \u2014 'The Spear Hero's men mean to cheat, Shield Hero-sama. The Queen would see fair play \u2014 use this.' Filo, gleeful \u2014 'Fast! Master, I'll go SO fast \u2014 weeee!' Naofumi, dry \u2014 'Tch. Win, Filo. Don't hold back.'\n[Axe Hero] A favored hero, {{user}} could be at Riyute for the spectacle \u2014 the whole region turns out for a Hero's race \u2014 free to wager, heckle, referee, or call out Motoyasu's cheating. The tax-grab is the kind of favored-hero overreach he might wave through or oppose; his stance is his. The world stages it and waits.",
    brief:"[EP11 — The Cart Race] Motoyasu seizes Riyute with harsh taxes; a Shadow-backed cart-race decides it, and Filo's speed wins Naofumi the village plus a carriage and trade permit. {{user}} can spectate, wager, or call out Motoyasu's cheating." },

  { ep:12,
    full:"[EP12 — Filo's Other Shape | Arc 4: Filo Rial] One morning Filo is gone from the cart and a winged woman stands in her place \u2014 a filolial queen with a fully adult humanoid form, bare and cheerfully unbothered by it. Cloth won't survive her shifting between shapes without magic thread spun from a rare crystal, so Naofumi clears the Alchemist's Cave alongside the magic-shop owner, downs a Nue for the crystal, and a tailor stitches Filo an outfit that changes with her. Kitted and provisioned, the party \u2014 Shield, sword, and filolial \u2014 sets out in earnest as traveling merchants.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Filo, guileless \u2014 'Master! Look, I'm a person now! Is it good? Can we go fast in the cart?' Raphtalia, flustered \u2014 'Hyaa\u2014?! Filo, put something ON! ...Naofumi-sama, don't just stand there!' the magic-shop owner, wry \u2014 'A Nue in that cave, Hero-sama. Nasty thing \u2014 mind the fire.' Naofumi, deadpan \u2014 'Clothes first. Questions later.'\n[Axe Hero] The Alchemist's Cave, the tailor, the crystal trade \u2014 all open to {{user}} and his party; the Axe Hero might clear the cave himself or cross Naofumi's cart on the road out of Castle Town. Where he travels next, and whether the Shield's odd little party is on that road, is his. The world offers, then waits.",
    brief:"[EP12 — Filo's Other Shape] Filo reveals her adult humanoid form; Naofumi clears the Alchemist's Cave (a Nue) for magic-thread clothing, and the party sets out as traveling merchants. {{user}} works the same cave and roads." },

  { ep:13,
    full:"[EP13 — On the Peddler's Road | Arc 5: Peddling] With cart and permit, Naofumi builds his peddling trade \u2014 first delivering rare medicine to a bedridden old woman who rallies at once. On the road he pulls a traveling accessory-merchant out of a bandit ambush, and in thanks the man teaches him simple spellcasting and accessory-crafting, then points him to work in Lerno Village, a day's ride on. Lerno is being swallowed by vines and plant-monsters: Motoyasu handed them a 'miracle seed' for their famine and it grew into a devouring BioPlant. Naofumi sells them weed-killer, takes the extermination contract, and destroys the core plant so the rest withers \u2014 then mutates its seed into a safe, crop-bearing strain and takes a share of the harvest.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): the old woman, frail and glad \u2014 'Bless you, Hero-sama... I can breathe again.' the accessory-merchant, earnest \u2014 'You saved my neck, Shield Hero-dono. Here \u2014 let me teach you a trade for it.' a Lerno farmer, desperate \u2014 'The Spear Hero-sama's gift, it \u2014 it won't stop growing! Please, Hero-sama!' Naofumi, mercantile \u2014 'Weed-killer's two silver a jar. The big plant costs extra.'\n[Axe Hero] The peddler's roads and cleanup contracts are open to the Axe Hero too \u2014 Motoyasu's runaway 'miracle seed' at Lerno is exactly the sort of favored-hero mess {{user}} could be hired to fix, or cause. Whether he shares a road, a job, or a crafting lesson with the scorned Shield is his. The world offers, then waits.",
    brief:"[EP13 — On the Peddler's Road] Naofumi peddles medicine, learns crafting and magic from a rescued merchant, and clears Lerno's runaway BioPlant (Motoyasu's 'miracle seed'), mutating it into a crop. {{user}} works the same roads and cleanup jobs." },

  { ep:14,
    full:"[EP14 — The Zombie Dragon | Arc 5: Peddling] Mirso Village sends for medicine, but Naofumi reads the truth fast: Ren slew a dragon nearby and left the carcass to rot, and the corruption is what's sickening the valley. When the party goes to clear it, the corpse heaves back up as a Zombie Dragon \u2014 and it swallows Filo whole. Something in Naofumi breaks; he reaches for the Shield of Wrath and unleashes it, tearing the dragon apart, but the curse's rage overflows and lashes Raphtalia before he can rein it in. Filo bursts free of the carcass, pressing a shard of the dragon's core into his hand. The Wrath's burn and Raphtalia's curse both need Castle Town's pure holy water.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): a Mirso elder, fearful \u2014 'The beast the Sword Hero-sama slew... it rose again, Hero-sama!' Raphtalia, strained under the curse \u2014 'Ku\u2014! Naofumi-sama, your arm \u2014 the Shield, it's eating you\u2014!' Filo, muffled then bursting free \u2014 'Mmph\u2014! Master! I'm okay \u2014 here, for you!' Naofumi, low and shaking with rage \u2014 'Give her back. Give. Her. BACK.'\n[Axe Hero] The favored heroes leave ruin behind them \u2014 Ren's abandoned dragon is one more mess on the roads {{user}} travels. The Axe Hero could take the same Mirso job, arrive on the Wrath-lit aftermath, or never cross it; and the sight of the Shield consumed by his own curse is a thing to witness, aid, or judge. The world burns and waits.",
    brief:"[EP14 — The Zombie Dragon] Ren's rotting dragon-corpse rises as a Zombie Dragon and swallows Filo; Naofumi's despair unleashes the Shield of Wrath, which kills it but curses Raphtalia. Filo bursts free with a core shard. {{user}} may cross the aftermath." },

  { ep:15,
    full:"[EP15 — Melty on the Road | Arc 5: Peddling] Bound for Castle Town and its holy water, the party meets a poised young noblewoman with long blue hair in twin-tails, traveling with a small escort; she takes to Filo on sight and within the hour the two are inseparable. She gives her name only as Melty and asks to travel together; Naofumi, wary but short a reason to refuse, agrees to see her safely to the capital. At Erhard's forge they upgrade their gear and the old smith delivers hard news: Raphtalia and Filo have hit the level cap and can't grow further without a class-up ceremony at the Dragon Hourglass.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Melty, courteous and warm \u2014 'Your filolial is wonderful! I'm Melty \u2014 might we travel together, Shield Hero-sama?' Filo, delighted \u2014 'Melty's my friend now! Master, can she ride in the cart? Please please please?' Erhard, gruff \u2014 'They've capped, kid. No more levels without a class-up at the Hourglass \u2014 and that I can't help you with.' Raphtalia, gentle \u2014 'She's kind, Naofumi-sama. ...Not everyone is like the palace.'\n[Axe Hero] Melty \u2014 secretly the second princess, though she keeps that quiet on the road \u2014 is the reformist, good-faith side of the crown, and she'd regard the favored Axe Hero far more warmly than the palace treats the Shield. {{user}} might share the road, the forge, or the Hourglass errand, or run his own. The world introduces her and waits.",
    brief:"[EP15 — Melty on the Road] The party meets the poised young noblewoman Melty (secretly the second princess), who bonds with Filo; Naofumi escorts her toward Castle Town's holy water, and Erhard reveals Raphtalia and Filo need a class-up to grow. {{user}} may share the road." },

  { ep:16,
    full:"[EP16 — The Second Princess | Arc 6: Third Wave] Back in Castle Town for the holy water, Naofumi is jumped in the street by Motoyasu \u2014 and Melty steps between them, revealing herself as the crown's second princess and heir to end it. But when Naofumi learns she's Malty's sister and Aultcray's daughter, he shuts her out on reflex, unable to trust the name. At the Church of the Four's Dragon Hourglass the clergy refuse Raphtalia and Filo's class-up \u2014 the Shield's party gets nothing here \u2014 so he upgrades their gear instead. A young Melromarc soldier trails after him, begging to join the Shield's party for the coming Wave; Naofumi puts him off, telling him to first raise real coin.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Motoyasu, hostile \u2014 'Hands off the princess, Naofumi! Haven't you done enough?' Melty, commanding for her years \u2014 'Enough! Spear Hero, stand down \u2014 that is an ORDER.' a Church-of-the-Four priest, cold \u2014 'The altar does not turn for the Shield. Take your beasts elsewhere.' the soldier, pleading \u2014 'Let me fight at your side, Shield Hero-sama! I'll get the coin, I swear it!' Naofumi, clipped \u2014 'Money first. Then we'll talk.'\n[Axe Hero] Where the Church of the Four bars the Shield from the altar, it would usher the favored Axe Hero through with blessings \u2014 {{user}} class-ups freely, and hopefuls like that soldier might sooner flock to him. Whether he notices the Shield turned away beside him, or steps between him and Motoyasu, is his. The world acts and waits.",
    brief:"[EP16 — The Second Princess] Motoyasu attacks; Melty reveals herself as heir to stop it, but Naofumi distrusts Malty's sister; the Church of the Four denies his class-up; a soldier begs to join (told to raise coin first). {{user}}, favored, class-ups freely and is courted by the same hopefuls." },

  { ep:17,
    full:"[EP17 — The Ruined North | Arc 6: Third Wave] Before the Wave, Naofumi's road takes him through a famine-struck northern territory \u2014 one Itsuki 'liberated' by toppling its corrupt governor, then left to collapse into worse poverty than before. Naofumi hands the starving people a BioPlant seed to feed themselves. On the way Ren and Itsuki corner him with a fresh accusation \u2014 that he's been stealing quest rewards from the Adventurer's Guild \u2014 until he picks their logic apart and clears himself. The soldier from Castle Town catches up, coin in hand as promised; Naofumi tells him to spend it on his own gear and takes him into the party.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Itsuki, self-righteous \u2014 'I freed these people from a tyrant. If they suffer now, that is hardly my concern.' Ren, flat accusation \u2014 'The guild's rewards keep vanishing. It's you, isn't it, Naofumi.' Naofumi, cutting \u2014 'You toppled a governor and left no one to run the grain stores. Genius. And I haven't touched your guild.' the soldier, earnest \u2014 'Every copper, Shield Hero-sama \u2014 just as you said!'\n[Axe Hero] The favored heroes' 'heroics' keep leaving wreckage \u2014 Itsuki's ruined north is a place {{user}} might pass, aid, or ignore. Ren and Itsuki would never level that theft charge at a fellow favored hero the way they do at the Shield; the Axe Hero sits on the accusers' side of that line unless he chooses otherwise. The world unfolds and waits.",
    brief:"[EP17 — The Ruined North] Naofumi feeds a famine-struck north that Itsuki wrecked, deflects Ren and Itsuki's theft accusation, and takes in the soldier who raised his coin. {{user}}, favored, sits on the accusers' side of the line unless he chooses otherwise." },

  { ep:18,
    full:"[EP18 — The Third Wave | Arc 6: Third Wave] The Dragon Hourglass empties and the game-mechanic warp seizes every Hero and party \u2014 {{user}} among them \u2014 and sets them down at the single red-skied rift. (Render the pull taking {{user}} and dropping him near the other Heroes at the front, then STOP for his action \u2014 the one time the world moves him.) Naofumi turns for the village to shield the smallfolk while Ren, Motoyasu, and Itsuki charge off and promptly bog down, squabbling over their clashing 'game knowledge' and unable to even find the boss. Naofumi finds it \u2014 a Soul Eater, far past the three of them \u2014 and barely drops it with a curse-series skill, yet the rift won't close. Then a woman in black and white steps from the tear: Glass, who overpowers even Naofumi with ease, only for the Wave-timer to run out and force her to withdraw. The next day the King demands to know how the Shield grew strong; Naofumi will only tell him if he kneels, and is thrown out for it.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Motoyasu, floundering \u2014 'The boss should be at the map's center! Ren, your intel's wrong!' a terrified villager \u2014 'Hyaa\u2014! They're through the wall! Hero-sama, please!' Glass, cold and courteous \u2014 'You are the only true Hero on this field. The rest are noise. Draw your shield.' Naofumi, grim \u2014 'Behind me. Move. Now.'\n[Axe Hero] The warp drops {{user}} at the rift with everyone else \u2014 the Axe Hero is on that battlefield whether he likes it or not. Charge the Soul Eater with the favored trio, break for the village beside the scorned Shield, or hold a flank with his own party \u2014 and Glass counts every Legendary Hero present as a target, {{user}} included. The rift is the scene's gravity; the world acts on him, then waits.",
    brief:"[EP18 — The Third Wave] The Hourglass warps all Heroes (incl. {{user}}) to the rift; the favored trio flounder, Naofumi downs the Soul Eater, and the otherworlder Glass overpowers him before the timer forces her out. The King ejects him for demanding he kneel. {{user}} is warped in, a target for Glass too." },

  { ep:19,
    full:"[EP19 — The Frame | Arc 7: Devil of the Shield] Denied the class-up, Naofumi sets out for demi-human-friendly Shieldfreeden on Erhard's advice. On the road Melty's own escort turns on her \u2014 they try to murder the princess while a magic recorder captures it, meaning to pin her death on the Shield. Naofumi cuts them down and saves her, but some assassins slip away with the doctored footage. Within the day the realm is papered with wanted posters and faked recordings casting his party as the villains \u2014 the Church of the Four's 'Devil of the Shield' campaign in full cry \u2014 and they go to ground, moving by back roads.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): the treacherous escort-captain, cold \u2014 'Forgive me, Princess \u2014 the Shield-devil's crime will be recorded right here.' Melty, shaken then steel \u2014 'You'd murder me and blame HIM? ...Stand down, all of you!' Raphtalia, fierce \u2014 'Get away from her \u2014 Naofumi-sama, the recorder!' Naofumi, grim \u2014 'Of course. Frame me for the princess too. Why not.'\n[Axe Hero] The 'Devil of the Shield' broadsheets flatter the favored \u2014 {{user}} is handed the propaganda, perhaps asked by the Church of the Four to help run the Shield down. Believe it, doubt it, join the hunt, or quietly warn the hunted: his read of the smear is his. The world circulates the lie and waits.",
    brief:"[EP19 — The Frame] Melty's escort tries to murder her on a magic recorder to frame the Shield; Naofumi saves her but the doctored footage spreads and the realm turns on his party. {{user}}, favored, is fed the propaganda \u2014 believe it, doubt it, or aid the hunted." },

  { ep:20,
    full:"[EP20 — The Flight | Arc 7: Devil of the Shield] The party runs for Shieldfreeden by back roads, Melty proving unexpectedly capable, until the other Heroes, Malty, and a column of soldiers corner them. Motoyasu, Ren, and Itsuki move to take them captive \u2014 while Malty simply tries to have them killed \u2014 and only the Queen's Shadows, striking from cover, get them clear. In the scramble a Shadow reaches Naofumi with new orders: turn from Shieldfreeden and make for Siltvelt, where the returning Queen means to meet him. One hard day of running, not a week.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Malty, shrill-sweet \u2014 'Don't bother capturing him \u2014 just kill the Shield-devil! Ufufu, no one will mourn.' Motoyasu, righteous \u2014 'Stand down, Naofumi! Hand over the princess and it'll go easier.' a Shadow, urgent \u2014 'This way, Shield Hero-sama \u2014 the Queen wants you in Siltvelt. Move!' Naofumi, breathless \u2014 'Tch \u2014 Filo, GO. Don't look back.'\n[Axe Hero] A realm-wide manhunt is a thing a favored hero can join, lead, or sit out. {{user}} might ride with the Heroes closing the net \u2014 or find the sight of four Heroes and an army hunting one Shield and a princess telling. Throw in, hang back, or tip the scales: his call. The world gives chase and waits.",
    brief:"[EP20 — The Flight] The Heroes, Malty, and soldiers corner the fugitives; the Shadows extract them and redirect them toward Siltvelt to meet the returning Queen. {{user}} can join the hunt, sit out, or tip the scales. (Travel compressed.)" },

  { ep:21,
    full:"[EP21 — Rabier's Dungeon | Arc 7: Devil of the Shield] Sheltered by a friendly noble, the party is betrayed when the Church-aligned Idol Rabier seizes their host for harboring the 'Devil of the Shield' \u2014 and Melty lets herself be taken to buy them time. Raphtalia reveals the horror: Rabier once owned and tortured her. In the rescue she faces her old tormentor at last; Rabier tumbles from his own window and is presumed dead. Freeing his tortured slaves, Raphtalia finds her surviving friend from home, Keel, and learns another of their village, Rifana, has died. The dying Rabier unseals a caged monster, the Tyrant Dragon Rex, which ravages the land until the ancient filolial queen Fitoria descends, destroys it, and bears the party off to her domain.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Idol Rabier, gloating \u2014 'The Shield-devil's pets... ohoho, I do so love breaking demi-humans.' Raphtalia, trembling then iron \u2014 'You. I remember you. Not this time \u2014 NEVER again.' Keel, hoarse \u2014 'R-Raphtalia? Is that \u2014 Bubba Shield came for us?!' Fitoria, imperious \u2014 'Enough. This beast dies, and then we talk, Shield Hero.'\n[Axe Hero] Rabier is a Church-of-the-Four noble who would wine and flatter a favored Hero even as he tortures demi-humans in his cellar \u2014 {{user}} could be his honored guest, stumble on the dungeon, or meet the Tyrant Dragon's rampage. Whether the Axe Hero dines with such men or breaks their doors is his. The world turns and waits.",
    brief:"[EP21 — Rabier's Dungeon] The Church-aligned Rabier (Raphtalia's old torturer) seizes their host; the rescue frees his slaves (Keel found, Rifana lost), Rabier falls to his death, and his unsealed Tyrant Dragon is destroyed by Fitoria, who takes the party to her domain. {{user}} may be Rabier's guest or the one who breaks his doors." },

  { ep:22,
    full:"[EP22 — Unite or Die | Arc 7: Devil of the Shield] In her domain Fitoria issues her ultimatum: unite the Heroes, or she will kill them all so the world can summon better ones. She duels Filo with Melty as hostage; Filo impresses her and is named the next filolial queen. Fitoria then delivers the party to Motoyasu to make peace \u2014 but he attacks on sight, certain Naofumi murdered Ren and Itsuki. As they fight, a devastating blast strikes them both: the Pope of the Church of the Four reveals himself, declares every Hero a 'fake,' and turns his relic on them to seize the realm for his god. Ren and Itsuki \u2014 secretly saved by the Shadows \u2014 arrive to reinforce, and the Heroes hold roughly even until Queen Mirellia returns and breaks the siege. Naofumi ends the Pope with a Wrath-Series skill, and is nearly killed by the cost.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Fitoria, grave \u2014 'Unite, Shield Hero, or I replace you all. Do not test me.' Motoyasu, wild \u2014 'You killed them! Ren, Itsuki \u2014 you MURDERED them, Naofumi!' the Pope of the Four, fanatic \u2014 'Fakes, all five! Kneel before your god \u2014 and the Shield-devil burns first!' Queen Mirellia, ice \u2014 'That is quite enough. Stand down, or be put down.'\n[Axe Hero] Fitoria's 'unite or die' judgment falls on ALL five \u2014 {{user}} is one of the Heroes she will cull if they won't cooperate. And the Pope's true design spares no one: once he brands every Hero a fake, the favored Axe Hero is as much a target as the Shield. Whether {{user}} stands with the others against the Pope \u2014 or the Pope's fire finally teaches him the Church's 'favor' was always conditional \u2014 is his. The world erupts and waits.",
    brief:"[EP22 — Unite or Die] Fitoria's 'unite or die' ultimatum crowns Filo her heir; delivered to Motoyasu, the Pope of the Four springs his coup branding all Heroes fakes; Ren/Itsuki reinforce, the Queen returns, and Naofumi ends the Pope with the Wrath Shield. Fitoria's judgment and the Pope's fire target {{user}} too." },

  { ep:23,
    full:"[EP23 — The Trial | Arc 8: Punishment] Naofumi wakes in the royal hospital, the Pope's blast having nearly killed him. Queen Mirellia has returned and exposed Malty and Aultcray; the King is dethroned and both stand trial. A slave crest set on Malty forces the truth out: she engineered the summoning of every Hero into Melromarc so rival nations could have none, fabricated the assault charge, tried to steal Raphtalia in a rigged duel, and plotted to murder her own sister Melty for the throne \u2014 all of which the doting King simply believed. The court finally sees the Shield was innocent all along. Aultcray still spits that he is a devil. The Queen places their sentence in Naofumi's hands and he condemns them to die \u2014 but at the scaffold, Malty's sincere, crest-quiet begging shows death would settle nothing, so he halts it and has Aultcray renamed 'Trash' and Malty 'Bitch' instead, stripped of rank and cast out.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Malty, crest-forced and unraveling \u2014 'I summoned them all \u2014 I lied about everything \u2014 stop, make it STOP!' King Aultcray, hollow and stubborn \u2014 'Do what you will. The Shield is still a devil.' Queen Mirellia, cold justice \u2014 'Their fate is yours to name, Shield Hero. Choose.' Naofumi, quiet and merciless \u2014 'Death's too kind. From now you're 'Trash.' And she's 'Bitch.' Bow.'\n[Axe Hero] Malty's confession lays it bare \u2014 {{user}}'s OWN summoning was part of her scheme to deny other nations their Heroes; as a favored hero he may have been one of the faces she smiled at. The trial and the scaffold are public. Where the Axe Hero stands \u2014 vindication, mercy, cold satisfaction, or indifference \u2014 is his. The world judges and waits.",
    brief:"[EP23 — The Trial] The returned Queen tries Malty and Aultcray; Malty's crest-forced confession clears Naofumi, and he spares them into the renamed 'Trash' and 'Bitch,' cast out. {{user}}'s own summoning is exposed as part of Malty's scheme." },

  { ep:24,
    full:"[EP24 — The Church of the Five | Arc 8: Punishment] In private the Queen gives Naofumi the harder truths: the chaos Malty caused by hoarding every Hero in one realm, and that it was her own Shadows who arranged for him to be sold a slave \u2014 though she never chose whom, and was as surprised as anyone that a demi-human of the Seaetto line became his first companion. Naofumi affirms he will keep working with Melromarc. At the Dragon Hourglass the discredited, anti-Shield Church of the Four is disbanded and replaced by the Church of the Five, which honors the Shield alongside the other four Holy Weapons at last; Raphtalia and Filo finally receive their class-up (their paths locked by Fitoria's lingering blessing on Filo), and Naofumi accepts the result.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Queen Mirellia, candid \u2014 'My Shadows led you to that tent, Shield Hero-sama \u2014 not to her, specifically. I will not pretend my hands are clean.' a Church-of-the-Five priest, reverent \u2014 'The altar turns for all five now, Hero-sama \u2014 the Shield included.' Raphtalia, moved \u2014 'A proper class-up, at last. ...Fufu, Filo, hold still.' Naofumi, grudging \u2014 'Fine. We keep working with Melromarc. For now.'\n[Axe Hero] When the Church of the Four collapses into the Church of the Five, the faith that once raised the four favored above the Shield is remade around all five \u2014 and the Axe Hero's place in the world's worship shifts with it. {{user}} might feel the ground move under his 'favor,' welcome the Shield's rise, or resent it. His response is his. The world reforms and waits.",
    brief:"[EP24 — The Church of the Five] The Queen's private truths; the Church of the Four falls and the Church of the Five rises honoring all five; Raphtalia and Filo class-up. {{user}}'s place in the reformed faith shifts." },

  { ep:25,
    full:"[EP25 — The Isles of Cal Mira | Arc 9: Cal Mira Island] The Queen sends the Heroes to the Cal Mira Archipelago, where an event sharply boosts experience. On the crossing \u2014 after Naofumi lets Raphtalia visit the ruins of her home village, lost in an early Wave \u2014 they fall in with two easygoing adventurers also bound for the isles, L'Arc and Therese. In Cal Mira the jovial Earl of Habenburg tours Naofumi's party while the other Heroes nurse their seasickness; Naofumi finds an ancient tablet that teaches a powerful party buff. They grind across the islands, teaming with L'Arc and Therese to great effect \u2014 and Naofumi notes L'Arc carries something very like a Legendary Weapon, but doesn't pry.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): L'Arc, breezy and warm \u2014 'Oi, kiddo! You and your crew fight well \u2014 drinks on me when we make port, eh?' Therese, serene \u2014 'The gems here sing so brightly... ufufu, I could stay forever.' the Earl of Habenburg, jovial \u2014 'Welcome, Hero-sama! The isles are yours \u2014 level to your heart's content.' Raphtalia, quiet at the ruins \u2014 'This was my home. ...Thank you for stopping, Naofumi-sama.'\n[Axe Hero] The Cal Mira event is open to every favored Hero \u2014 {{user}} has as much reason to be on the isles leveling as anyone, and L'Arc and Therese befriend easily. Whether the Axe Hero drinks with them, trains apart, or keeps his distance is his. The world welcomes him and waits.",
    brief:"[EP25 — The Isles of Cal Mira] At the exp-boosting archipelago Naofumi befriends the adventurers L'Arc and Therese and finds a powerful buff-tablet; L'Arc secretly carries a Legendary-like weapon. {{user}}, favored, is here too and may befriend them." },

  { ep:26,
    full:"[EP26 — The Archipelago Wave | Arc 9: Cal Mira Island] Filo finds an underwater Dragon Hourglass warning of a Wave at the isles within days, and it breaks soon after. In the fighting L'Arc and Therese reveal staggering power, one-shotting the Wave boss \u2014 then turn on Naofumi: to save their own world, they must kill this world's Legendary Heroes. L'Arc fights with real honor and skill, and Glass arrives to back them. Naofumi is cornered until Rishia and the Queen reinforce him and detonate a cask of rucolu fruit, whose fumes intoxicate everyone present \u2014 except the taste-dead, intoxication-proof Naofumi. With Glass too drunk to stand, the three otherworlders withdraw. The battle lays bare just how weak Ren, Motoyasu, and Itsuki truly are.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): L'Arc, grim now \u2014 'Nothing personal, kiddo. Your world or mine \u2014 and I choose mine.' Glass, cold \u2014 'Fall here, Shield Hero. It is simply necessary.' Therese, reluctant \u2014 'Forgive me... I truly did enjoy your company.' Rishia, panicking but game \u2014 'Fueee\u2014! The rucolu, Naofumi-sama \u2014 light it NOW!'\n[Axe Hero] The Wave warps {{user}} to the isles' front with the rest \u2014 and L'Arc, Therese, and Glass have come to kill this world's Legendary Heroes, so the Axe Hero is squarely on their list. Unlike Naofumi he is NOT immune to the rucolu haze, so the fumes take him too if he's near. Fight them, fall drunk in the smoke, or be spared by L'Arc's odd honor: his call. The world reels and waits.",
    brief:"[EP26 — The Archipelago Wave] L'Arc, Therese, and Glass turn on the heroes (to save their world they must kill this one's); rucolu fumes rout them (Naofumi's immune), exposing the trio's weakness. {{user}} is a target too \u2014 and not rucolu-immune." },

  { ep:27,
    full:"[EP27 — The Cast-Off | Arc 9: Cal Mira Island] In the Wave's aftermath, seeking another companion, Naofumi finds Motoyasu trying to console a distraught woman \u2014 Rishia, lately of Itsuki's party. Jealous of how useful she'd proven in the Wave, Itsuki's teammates framed her and had her cast out. Naofumi confronts Itsuki, who coldly refuses to take her back or admit any wrong. When despair drives Rishia to the cliff's edge to end it, Filo snatches her from the fall \u2014 and Naofumi offers her a place and a promise to make her strong. She takes it.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Rishia, broken then flickering \u2014 'I'm useless... everyone says so... fueee...' Itsuki, dismissive \u2014 'She was dead weight. I act only in the name of justice \u2014 and justice has no place for her.' Motoyasu, uncharacteristically gentle \u2014 'Oi, don't say that. You're not \u2014 someone, help her!' Naofumi, blunt but not unkind \u2014 'You're not useless. You're untrained. Come with me \u2014 I'll fix the second part.'\n[Axe Hero] Rishia's expulsion is the kind of cast-off loyalty the Axe Hero could just as easily take in \u2014 recruitment is the volunteer's choice, and she might attach to {{user}} instead if he'd have her. Whether he confronts Itsuki, catches her himself, or leaves it to the Shield is his. The world breaks a little and waits.",
    brief:"[EP27 — The Cast-Off] Itsuki's jealous party framed and expelled the capable Rishia; near suicide, Filo saves her and Naofumi recruits her with a promise of strength. {{user}} could take her in instead \u2014 volunteer's choice." },

  { ep:28,
    full:"[EP28 — The Instructors | Arc 11: Spirit Turtle] The clash with the otherworlders makes plain the Heroes must grow far stronger. Queen Mirellia opens Melromarc's stockpile to Naofumi and assigns combat instructors: the sword-knight Eclair Seaetto, now governing Raphtalia's home region, and Elrasla Ragnarok, the aged last master of the Hengen Muso life-force style. The training bites at once \u2014 Eclair beats Ren in a duel despite not being a Hero \u2014 but Ren, Motoyasu, and Itsuki keep dodging the sessions, while Naofumi's team, Rishia above all, take to Hengen Muso fast. To get the Heroes moving, the Queen strikes a bargain: they may leave if they'll investigate the mysterious attacks springing up across the world.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Eclair, upright and stern \u2014 'Rank means nothing if you won't lift your blade for what's right. Again, Sword Hero-sama \u2014 guard up.' Elrasla, wry and merciless \u2014 'Levels? Bah. Let an old woman show you what Life Force can do, boy.' Rishia, blooming \u2014 'I \u2014 I did it! Elrasla-sensei, I actually did it!' Ren, sullen \u2014 'This is a waste of time. Tch.'\n[Axe Hero] Eclair and Elrasla drill every Hero who shows up \u2014 {{user}} can take the life-force training to heart like Naofumi's crew or blow it off like the favored three. Hengen Muso bypasses raw levels, so what the Axe Hero makes of it could matter later. His diligence is his. The world instructs and waits.",
    brief:"[EP28 — The Instructors] The Queen assigns Eclair and Elrasla to train the Heroes in Hengen Muso; the favored three dodge it, Naofumi's team (esp. Rishia) excel, and the Queen frees them to investigate mysterious attacks. {{user}} can take the training seriously or skip it." },

  { ep:29,
    full:"[EP29 — The Spirit Tortoise | Arc 11: Spirit Turtle] Investigating the attacks, Naofumi's party finds Lerno Village overrun by parasitic familiars and barely saves Keel from being taken over by one. The Shadows soon name the source: a rampaging Guardian Beast, the Spirit Tortoise, whose swarming familiars are savaging the world. They race east \u2014 a hard day's travel \u2014 and find the land in ruins, the dead uncounted, and the other Heroes vanished. Naofumi, Raphtalia, Filo, Eclair, and Elrasla throw everything into it and behead the colossal Tortoise; atop its shell they find a temple, and within it a warning left by a Hero of a past age.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Keel, straining against the parasite \u2014 'Ku\u2014! Get it off, Bubba Shield \u2014 it's in my HEAD\u2014!' a Shadow, grim \u2014 'A Guardian Beast, Shield Hero-sama. The Spirit Tortoise. It will not stop.' Eclair, awed \u2014 'That... that is the size of a mountain.' Elrasla, dry \u2014 'Then we take the mountain's head off. Mind your footing, boy.'\n[Axe Hero] As a Legendary Hero, {{user}} is drawn into the Guardian-Beast crisis too \u2014 among the defenders racing east, or, like the favored three, vanished in its shadow. And the Spirit Tortoise waking is a reminder the other Guardians still sleep, the White Tiger \u2014 the Axe Hero's own \u2014 among them. Where {{user}} stands is his. The world quakes and waits.",
    brief:"[EP29 — The Spirit Tortoise] Parasitic familiars (Keel nearly taken) lead to the rampaging Guardian Beast, the Spirit Tortoise; the party races east and beheads it, finding a past hero's warning in the shell-temple. {{user}} is entangled too; his own guardian, the White Tiger, still sleeps." },

  { ep:30,
    full:"[EP30 — Ost and the Corruption | Arc 11: Spirit Turtle] Hunting the missing Heroes among the leftover familiars, the party meets Ost Horai, a gentle woman who reveals she is the Spirit Tortoise's own familiar \u2014 and that the Beast is not truly dead; something has corrupted it. It heaves back up in a worse form and turns to march on Melromarc. The ancient Fitoria arrives to hold its vast body while Naofumi's force goes inside to destroy the head and heart at once. After a brutal, failed first attempt, they finally shatter the head and seal the heart together, stilling the Beast \u2014 but the thing that corrupted it waits deeper in the core.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Ost, serene and sorrowful \u2014 'I was made to end hated and alone, Hero-sama. Help me stop what I've become... please.' Fitoria, commanding \u2014 'I will hold the body. You \u2014 get inside and end this, Shield Hero.' Raphtalia, resolute \u2014 'Head and heart together, Naofumi-sama. On your mark.' Naofumi, focused \u2014 'Ost, guide us. Everyone \u2014 we hit it as one.'\n[Axe Hero] Bringing down a Guardian Beast takes every Hero who will stand \u2014 {{user}} could be inside the Tortoise with the strike-team, holding the line beside Fitoria, or absent while the Shield does the work. Ost, the doomed familiar, treats even a favored Hero as a possible friend rather than a master. What the Axe Hero gives this fight is his. The world heaves and waits.",
    brief:"[EP30 — Ost and the Corruption] Ost, the Tortoise's familiar, reveals it's corrupted, not dead; it regenerates and marches on Melromarc; Fitoria holds it while the party destroys head and heart together. {{user}} may join the strike or the line." },

  { ep:31,
    full:"[EP31 — The Core | Arc 11: Spirit Turtle] Deep in the Tortoise's core the party finds the three missing Heroes drained and captive, their energy siphoned by a sneering scientist named Kyo, wielder of a stolen Vassal Book. He outmatches them \u2014 until L'Arc, Therese, and Glass arrive, their worlds' feud set aside for this. Together, and only through Ost guiding Naofumi's Liberation-class magic and Rishia's hidden power surging at the brink, they break Kyo, who seizes the gathered energy and flees through a portal to his own world. With the core destroyed, Ost begins to fade; she bids the party a grateful farewell, asks them to return the Tortoise's energy to buy the world time, and grants Naofumi a Legendary Hero's rare gift \u2014 passage between worlds. As she dies, Naofumi and L'Arc's party cross the portal after Kyo.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Kyo, contemptuous \u2014 'Lives, souls, worlds \u2014 all just data for the experiment. Kukuku... die quietly.' Glass, allied now \u2014 'A truce, Shield Hero. This one threatens every world.' Ost, fading and glad \u2014 'Thank you... for proving I was more than a monster. Go \u2014 bring the energy home.' Rishia, blazing past her limit \u2014 'I won't let you \u2014 hraaah!'\n[Axe Hero] The captive, drained Heroes could as easily include {{user}} \u2014 or the Axe Hero could be one of the few still standing to break them free. Kyo counts every Hero as raw material; L'Arc's crew now fight beside their old targets against him. Whether {{user}} is in that core, and whether he takes Ost's cross-world road after Kyo, is his. The world tears open and waits.",
    brief:"[EP31 — The Core] Kyo siphons the captive heroes' energy; L'Arc's group allies with Naofumi, and Ost's Liberation magic + Rishia break Kyo, who flees between worlds. Dying Ost grants Naofumi cross-world passage. {{user}} may be a captive or a rescuer." },

  { ep:32,
    full:"[EP32 — The Lord of the Ruins | Arc 12: Rebuilding Arc Part 1] Back from the otherworld, Naofumi releases the Spirit Tortoise's energy, buying the world months before the next Wave. As his reward he takes lordship of the ruined territory that holds Raphtalia's home village, and asks the Slave Trader to track down every surviving Lurolona villager sold into slavery. He finds the village untouched after months \u2014 its governor, Eclair, would rather drill soldiers than rebuild \u2014 so he brings in Melty to run it properly, feeds it with BioPlant crops, and puts tamed monsters to the labor. Then slave-hunters raid the fledgling settlement, hoping to seize Lurolona demi-humans of their own.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Melty, businesslike \u2014 'Leave the ledgers and grain to me, Shield Hero-sama \u2014 you're hopeless at governing.' Eclair, sheepish \u2014 'I... may have prioritized training over the rebuilding. My apologies, Lord Iwatani.' Raphtalia, hopeful \u2014 'My village, alive again... Naofumi-sama, we can really do this.' a slave-hunter, sneering \u2014 'Fresh Lurolona stock, all in one place? Ohoho \u2014 grab them, boys!'\n[Axe Hero] A favored Hero could be granted lands of his own too \u2014 {{user}} might build a domain in parallel, recruit through the same Slave Trader, or lend a hand (or not) as the raiders hit the Shield's village. How the Axe Hero uses this rare lull \u2014 building, indulging, or roaming \u2014 is his. The world rebuilds and waits.",
    brief:"[EP32 — The Lord of the Ruins] Made a lord, Naofumi rebuilds Raphtalia's village with Melty governing and BioPlant/monster labor, and seeks the scattered Lurolona survivors as slave-hunters raid. {{user}} could build his own domain in the lull." },

  { ep:33,
    full:"[EP33 — The Coliseum | Arc 12: Rebuilding Arc Part 1] Told the Lurolona survivors have been priced sky-high (because the 'Shield Hero' is buying them all) and funneled to Zeltoble, Naofumi heads there and enters the coliseum's team battles for fast coin, backed by old partners like the Accessory Merchant. His team climbs the ranks until it's matched against the crowd favorite 'Nadia' \u2014 a brutal fight, until Raphtalia recognizes her as Sadeena, the Orca-demi-human 'big sister' of her old village, who promptly throws the match. The furious crowd forces an immediate bout against the champion, Murder Pierrot, whom they beat; with his backers' leverage Naofumi then breaks the crooked promoter and frees Sadeena's slave crest \u2014 learning she too had been trying to buy back the Lurolona survivors.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Sadeena, sultry and delighted \u2014 'Ara ara~ little Raphtalia? All grown and swinging a sword at big sis? Fufu \u2014 then I surrender, sugar.' the crooked promoter, oily \u2014 'A thrown match?! The crowd wants blood \u2014 send in Murder Pierrot!' the Accessory Merchant, shrewd \u2014 'Win this and the promoter's ours, Hero-sama. Leverage.' Raphtalia, stunned \u2014 'Sadeena-neesan... you're ALIVE?!'\n[Axe Hero] Zeltoble's coliseum is open coin and open recruiting for any fighter \u2014 the Axe Hero included \u2014 and the same underworld that hides Lurolona slaves and coliseum champions is there for {{user}} to work. Whether he fights for a name of his own, crosses the Shield's team, or hunts his own companions here is his. The world roars and waits.",
    brief:"[EP33 — The Coliseum] In Zeltoble's coliseum Naofumi fights his way up, reunites with and frees the Orca demi-human Sadeena (who threw their match), and beats the champion Murder Pierrot. {{user}} can fight, recruit, or make a name here too." },

  { ep:34,
    full:"[EP34 — The White Tiger Siblings | Arc 12: Rebuilding Arc Part 1] Combing the Zeltoble trader's stock, Naofumi buys two more slaves: a deathly ill Hakuko \u2014 White Tiger \u2014 demi-human woman named Atla, and her brother Fohl, and pours care into curing the illness no one else could. As Atla mends, both swear themselves to him utterly. Taking them to Castle Town to reset their levels, the party crosses paths with Trash, who reacts with strange, stricken recognition \u2014 they are the kin of his long-lost sister and the son of his old enemy. Murder Pierrot turns up at the village and is turned away, and word comes from the Queen: bring in Motoyasu, who has run amok.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Atla, serene and absolute \u2014 'I can see your heart, Naofumi-sama \u2014 far kinder than you pretend. I will never leave your side.' Fohl, gruff and fierce \u2014 'Lay one hand on my sister and I'll break it off. ...But you saved her. So I'm yours.' Trash, shaken \u2014 'Those eyes... you are... no. It cannot be.' Naofumi, wary \u2014 'Rest, Atla. You're not dying on me after all that.'\n[Axe Hero] The White Tiger is the Axe Hero's OWN Guardian Beast \u2014 so the Hakuko siblings' bloodline runs parallel to {{user}}'s cosmology, and Byakko may stir toward its Hero as its kin surface. The same trader's stock and coliseum underworld are open to him; and where Atla and Fohl choose to attach is the volunteers' call, not any hero's. What the Axe Hero makes of the White Tiger tie is his. The world turns and waits.",
    brief:"[EP34 — The White Tiger Siblings] Naofumi buys and cures the Hakuko (White Tiger) siblings Atla and Fohl, who swear loyalty; Trash reacts to his estranged kin; the Queen asks Naofumi to capture the runaway Motoyasu. The White Tiger is {{user}}'s own guardian \u2014 the bloodline ties to Byakko." },

  { ep:35,
    full:"[EP35 — Rat and the Dragon Egg | Arc 13: Rebuilding Arc Part 2] Sure now that the Heroes aren't the only real threat, Naofumi's party trains in earnest \u2014 above all in the life-force art of Hengen Muso \u2014 and he visits Erhard to order materials for Raphtalia's Vassal Katana. Back at the village an eccentric alchemist, Rat, a Faubrey exile, has arrived and offers her research and monster-craft; Naofumi accepts, and she reworks his BioPlant into living housing for the settlement. Among gifts sent by Shield-revering nations like Siltvelt and Shieldfreeden is a dragon egg \u2014 and with Rat and the beast-keeper Wyndia's help, Naofumi raises it, naming the hatchling Gaelion.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Rat, brisk and mad-scientist bright \u2014 'Fascinating specimens, Hero-sama \u2014 let me run a few tests. Your BioPlant will make lovely housing.' Wyndia, blunt and tender \u2014 'The egg's healthy. Be good to him \u2014 he's family now.' Raphtalia, warm \u2014 'A Vassal Katana of my own... thank you, Naofumi-sama.' Naofumi, dry \u2014 'Gaelion. Try not to eat the villagers.'\n[Axe Hero] Everything Naofumi builds here, {{user}} can build in parallel \u2014 commission Rat's monster-craft, raise a beast of his own, or have Erhard forge and feed new abilities into his Axe. Siltvelt and Shieldfreeden revere the Shield, but the wider world still favors the four, {{user}} among them \u2014 how he spends this lull, building or indulging, is his. The world settles and waits.",
    brief:"[EP35 — Rat and the Dragon Egg] The party trains in Hengen Muso; the alchemist Rat joins (BioPlant housing), and a gifted dragon egg is raised as Gaelion with Wyndia's help. {{user}} can build his own base, monster, and Axe upgrades in the lull." },

  { ep:36,
    full:"[EP36 — The Vassal Katana | Arc 13: Rebuilding Arc Part 2] Naofumi returns to Erhard's forge, and there Raphtalia's Vassal Katana drinks in a new ability from a blade the old smith has forged \u2014 weapon and wielder both a step stronger for the lull. The village grows behind them, the next Wave still months out, and for once the road ahead is theirs to shape rather than merely survive.\nVoice anchors (vary freely; honorifics/tics; never voice {{user}}): Erhard, gruff-proud \u2014 'Forged it myself, kid. Let the Katana chew on that \u2014 should wake something new in it.' Raphtalia, feeling the change \u2014 'It's... humming. I can feel a new skill, Naofumi-sama.' Naofumi, almost soft \u2014 'Good. You've earned it. ...All of you have.'\n[Axe Hero] The same forge and the same rare lull are the Axe Hero's to use \u2014 {{user}} can have Erhard feed a new ability into his Axe, or spend the quiet however he likes before the Wave clock turns again. What he builds toward, and who he has become by now, is his. The world breathes out and waits.",
    brief:"[EP36 — The Vassal Katana] At Erhard's forge Raphtalia's Vassal Katana absorbs a new ability; the village thrives in the lull before the next Wave. {{user}} can upgrade his own Axe and shape the quiet." }
];

